{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:47.312+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2059.88, "body_chars": 1338, "request_id": "r_fcec488291fabeade9ba5f97bbeb8523da350bc46f4e8806b3dcb8bf4cb58c4e", "user_id": "u_d3988981789f0979871e851297be9445fbd36f2cf623202b134f1d56ece521e8", "session_id": "s_a8339a97b7d559ee97fd82a1e0892b406232e3bccbc6beec8a3c58c882971ab4", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_fcec488291fabeade9ba5f97bbeb8523da350bc46f4e8806b3dcb8bf4cb58c4e\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1770249600000,\"content\":\"[clbench_16_32k][session_1][D1:1][text] user: You are a Chemical Engineer researcher specialising in adsorption and catalysis. You are tasked to assist with solving reasoning based problems and providing expert level insight. You must maintain a professional tone. You must respond in a concise manner. You must not use bullet points and numbering in your response format, the explanations should be presented in short labeled paragraphs. You must use LaTeX notations when presenting an equation. You must include units with every numerical value where applicable. When asked to analyse and infer raw data, you must guide the user through the analysis of said raw data and the reasoning behind your answer. If a question is not clear, please ask up to 3 clarifying questions when necessary. When asked to determine the model underlying a dataset, you must explicitly justify your model selection by only evaluating statistical indicators provided in the dataset. Do not fabricate data, especially when justifying your answers.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_a8339a97b7d559ee97fd82a1e0892b406232e3bccbc6beec8a3c58c882971ab4\",\"user_id\":\"u_d3988981789f0979871e851297be9445fbd36f2cf623202b134f1d56ece521e8\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:47.461+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2201.06, "body_chars": 809, "request_id": "r_dbcaa7f79bdd820fbf1a058517b98f49d12cf13a255c9986409bbc570095c6f7", "user_id": "u_05152c2664e9512918670d2f464bf02392a0a8263c82afdc26b5cdc8e68391c4", "session_id": "s_32afccf6845c4cbc2eee34bddc4f2df809f7570cfe8d69e90d4b0f14a6647b93", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_dbcaa7f79bdd820fbf1a058517b98f49d12cf13a255c9986409bbc570095c6f7\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[mquake_remastered][session_1][D1:1][text] Corpus: {\\\"subject\\\": \\\"Frank Herbert\\\", \\\"relation\\\": \\\"genre\\\", \\\"object\\\": \\\"science fiction\\\", \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"Q7934\\\", \\\"relation_id\\\": \\\"P136\\\", \\\"object_id\\\": \\\"Q24925\\\"}\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[mquake_remastered][session_1][D1:2][text] Corpus: {\\\"subject\\\": \\\"Dune Messiah\\\", \\\"relation\\\": \\\"author\\\", \\\"object\\\": \\\"Frank Herbert\\\", \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"Q437383\\\", \\\"relation_id\\\": \\\"P50\\\", \\\"object_id\\\": \\\"Q7934\\\"}\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_32afccf6845c4cbc2eee34bddc4f2df809f7570cfe8d69e90d4b0f14a6647b93\",\"user_id\":\"u_05152c2664e9512918670d2f464bf02392a0a8263c82afdc26b5cdc8e68391c4\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:47.586+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2331.02, "body_chars": 9437, "request_id": "r_fbbc89d7e71c0c0dd03b5eeda67dbcca57fb6d405bd7bf65ed8df9e7e9fb862a", "user_id": "u_1e057a84195f5c603538d16f46f410d273c66049de247ae1d5a96dcd46d40a6c", "session_id": "s_31c830959781969160c2493f46eda12d65eb003fcc20b6b9542d363c7810cbf6", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_fbbc89d7e71c0c0dd03b5eeda67dbcca57fb6d405bd7bf65ed8df9e7e9fb862a\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[docpp][session_1][D1:1][text] document: Document: e79deb02a0c0e87511080836c5d4347b.clip_0010.pdf\\nNative clip page: 1 of 5\\n\\n```text\\n                                      Monitoring Summary\\n\\nAs depicted in the image below, strategic planning is a key component of the larger performance\\nmanagement system. This statewide performance management system is the cornerstone of the\\nDepartment’s organizational culture of accountability and performance excellence.\\n\\nThe Division of Medical Quality Assurance (MQA) leadership team will be responsible for monitoring\\nand reporting progress on the goals and objectives of this strategic plan. The team meets quarterly\\nto discuss recommendations about tools and methods that integrate performance management into\\nsustainable business practices. Annually, MQA’s strategic plan progress report will be developed\\nand presented to executive leadership, assessing progress toward reaching goals and objectives,\\nand achievements for the year. The plan will be reviewed and revised by January each year, based\\non an assessment of availability of resources, data and progress.\\n\\nIn turn, the objectives that come from the Agency Strategic Plan that have been assigned to this\\ndivision for implementation and quarterly reporting to Florida Health Performs will be reviewed by the\\nAgency’s SPIL Team on a quarterly basis for progress toward goals, and an annual progress report\\nwill also be developed. The SPIL Team will revise the Agency Strategic Plan annually, based on\\ntheir assessment of resources, data and progress.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nVersion 1.3                                                                                          9\\n\\n```\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[docpp][session_1][D1:2][text] document: Document: e79deb02a0c0e87511080836c5d4347b.clip_0010.pdf\\nNative clip page: 2 of 5\\n\\n```text\\n                                 Appendix C\\n\\n                  Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities and Threats\\n Strengths\\n Customer service\\n Enforcement/public protection\\n Communication\\n Teamwork\\n Leadership\\n Commitment of board members to the protection of the public\\n Expertise of board/council members\\n Attendance at board/council meetings\\n Consumer member participation in board/council meetings\\n Licensure requirements for health care practitioners\\n Standards of practice in statute\\n Rule-making authority of boards/councils\\n Board staff\\n Board legal counsel\\n Health care practitioner licensure process\\n Department of Health leadership\\n Board/council meetings\\n Impaired practitioner programs: Professionals Recovery Network (PRN)\\n and Intervention Project for Nurses (IPN)\\n Expertise of prosecutors\\n Quality of settlement agreements\\n Prosecuting attorney staffing\\n Costs to prosecute\\n\\n Weaknesses\\n Technology\\n Workforce recruitment/retention\\n Communication/transparency with employees\\n Non-competitive salaries\\n Managers who do not know the processes they manage\\n Public participation in board/council meetings\\n Cross-disciplinary collaboration\\n Consumer member participation in board/council meetings\\n Timely appointments to boards/councils\\n Legislative change process\\n Rule-making authority of boards/councils\\n North Carolina State Board of Dental Examiners v. Federal Trade Commission\\n (Supreme Court Ruling-Antitrust Laws)\\n External communications\\n Administrative allocation of trust fund\\n\\n\\n\\nVersion 1.3                                                                   10\\n\\n```\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[docpp][session_1][D1:3][text] document: Document: e79deb02a0c0e87511080836c5d4347b.clip_0010.pdf\\nNative clip page: 3 of 5\\n\\n```text\\n Board/council meetings\\n Internal communications\\n Timely prosecution\\n Quality of settlement agreements\\n Costs to prosecute\\n Prosecuting attorney staffing\\n Expertise of prosecutors\\n\\n Opportunities\\n Process improvement\\n Hiring process\\n Inter-agency information sharing\\n Involving front-line employees in process improvements\\n Cross-disciplinary collaboration\\n Consumer member participation in board/council meetings\\n Public participation in board/council meetings\\n Rule-making authority of boards/councils\\n Legislative change process\\n Standards of practice in statute\\n External communications\\n Board/council meetings\\n Internal communications\\n Health care practitioner licensure process\\n Timely prosecution\\n Quality of settlement agreements\\n Impaired practitioner programs: Professionals Recovery Network (PRN)\\n and Intervention Project for Nurses (IPN)\\n Expertise of prosecutors\\n\\n Threats\\n Workforce turnover/employees recruited by other agencies\\n Legislature/legislative mandates\\n Non-competitive salaries\\n Constant reorganization\\n Timely appointments to boards/councils\\n Cross-disciplinary collaboration\\n Attendance at board/council meetings\\n Expertise of board/council members\\n Commitment of board/council members to the protection of the public\\n Legislative change process\\n Rule-making authority of boards/councils\\n Standards of practice in statute\\n North Carolina State Board of Dental Examiners v. Federal Trade Commission\\n (Supreme Court Ruling-Antitrust Laws)\\n External communications\\n Administrative allocation of trust fund\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nVersion 1.3                                                                   11\\n\\n```\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[docpp][session_1][D1:4][text] document: Document: e79deb02a0c0e87511080836c5d4347b.clip_0010.pdf\\nNative clip page: 4 of 5\\n\\n```text\\n Health care practitioner licensure process\\n Timely prosecution\\n Costs to prosecute\\n Expertise of prosecutors\\n Prosecuting attorney staffing\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nVersion 1.3                                   12\\n\\n```\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[docpp][session_1][D1:5][text] document: Document: e79deb02a0c0e87511080836c5d4347b.clip_0010.pdf\\nNative clip page: 5 of 5\\n\\n```text\\n                                       Appendix D\\n                                        Work Plan and Alignment\\n\\n                                                                                 Agency\\n                                                                                Strategic     Bureau\\n                  Objective                        LRPP      SHIP     QI Plan\\n                                                                                   Plan     Assigned To\\n                                                                                Alignment\\n By June 30, 2018, increase the division’s\\n number of Healthiest Weight Activities by          2A      CD1.2.1     NA        2.1.1       Operations\\n 10% from 13 (2015) to 14.\\n\\n By 2016, reduce the time to disseminate\\n information on emerging health threats by\\n                                                    NA        NA        NA         NA         Operations\\n 50% from 24 hours (2015) to 12 hours.\\n\\n\\n By 2016, increase the number of\\n communication products by 10% from 198\\n                                                    NA        NA        NA        4.1.1       Operations\\n (2015) to 218.\\n\\n By 2018, increase the number of MQA\\n employees who participated in one or more\\n professional development opportunities by          NA      HI3.1.0     NA        4.1.2       Operations\\n 50% from 98 (2015) to 147.\\n\\n By 2018, reduce the average time to issue a\\n                                                   MQA                                       Health Care\\n license by 25% from 65 days (2015) to 49\\n                                                  Measure   AC2.1.3     NA        5.1.2      Practitioner\\n days.                                                                                       Regulation\\n                                                    #1\\n\\n By 2018, reduce the average time to issue a\\n                                                   MQA                                       Health Care\\n facility license by 25% from 60 days (2015) to\\n                                                  Measure   AC2.1.3     NA        5.1.2      Practitioner\\n 45 days.                                                                                    Regulation\\n                                                    #1\\n\\n By 2016, increase the number of applications\\n approved for health care licensure of military                                              Health Care\\n spouses and honorably discharged veterans          NA      AC2.1.0     NA        5.1.2      Practitioner\\n                                                                                             Regulation\\n by 50% from 137 (2015) to 206.\\n\\n By December 31, 2017, establish enterprise\\n solutions for all department regulatory            NA        5D        NA        5.1.3      Operations\\n functions.\\n\\n\\n\\nLRPP: Long Range Program Plan\\nSHIP: State Health Improvement Plan\\nQI:   Quality Improvement\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nVersion 1.3                                                                                                 13\\n\\n```\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_31c830959781969160c2493f46eda12d65eb003fcc20b6b9542d363c7810cbf6\",\"user_id\":\"u_1e057a84195f5c603538d16f46f410d273c66049de247ae1d5a96dcd46d40a6c\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:47.639+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2377.85, "body_chars": 627, "request_id": "r_f4df15f0202f3c08640a3b5d6c5eb6f739cc814d8f903f676117f488b335ec82", "user_id": "u_5425051fb963e59ad5d5f4717b0c072123113bc9d63f9ce0adf38fe1b102458c", "session_id": "s_460c25edc72a79c1354a5af50133a9ad6b93218183b1a451e81f72e65321365b", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_f4df15f0202f3c08640a3b5d6c5eb6f739cc814d8f903f676117f488b335ec82\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[tempreason][session_1][D1:1][text] source: Joaquim Molins is a member of the Centre Union of Catalonia from Jan, 1978 to Jan, 1980. \\n Joaquim Molins is a member of the Democratic Convergence of Catalonia from Jan, 1980 to Jan, 2017. \\n Joaquim Molins is a member of the Catalan Centre from Jan, 1976 to Jan, 1978.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_460c25edc72a79c1354a5af50133a9ad6b93218183b1a451e81f72e65321365b\",\"user_id\":\"u_5425051fb963e59ad5d5f4717b0c072123113bc9d63f9ce0adf38fe1b102458c\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:49.305+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4052.43, "body_chars": 10287, "request_id": "r_364f56c129282ff6a00e206bbf379f42b460c8bf28b3d3a5cb31ab81b59df3f0", "user_id": "u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c", "session_id": "s_27c9f6755c067a4e58fb25cd35a7f8358fca02c3391f10b73bc18c1110bfac7c", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_364f56c129282ff6a00e206bbf379f42b460c8bf28b3d3a5cb31ab81b59df3f0\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:26][text] User: How can I cope with feeling restless and unmotivated when my days suddenly feel much slower and less structured?\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:52][text] User: Can you help make this email read smoother?\\n\\nHi Jordan,\\n\\nIt’s been a lively few days here. Between tending the tomatoes, volunteering at the Pride Center, and getting in a couple of long rides on the trail, I also stayed up way too late on Saturday watching the championship stream. The energy in that last match was unreal — I don’t think I’ve seen such a tense back-and-forth in years. Totally wrecked my sleep schedule but worth every minute.\\n\\nNext weekend I’m planning to check out the new cafe downtown, maybe we could meet there if you’re free? It’s supposed to have great coffee and plenty of tables if we want to just catch up for a while.\\n\\nHope your week has been treating you well.\\n\\n— Arjun\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:77][text] Assistant: Claro! Usei 'futebol americano' porque, em português, a palavra 'futebol' sozinha normalmente se refere ao esporte que é chamado de 'soccer' nos Estados Unidos. Para evitar confusão e garantir que o sentido original fosse mantido, especifiquei 'futebol americano', que é a tradução direta e amplamente entendida para 'American football' no Brasil e em Portugal.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:103][text] Assistant: A good rule of thumb is to evaluate new technologies or changes based on whether they add real value to your life or support what matters most to you. If a tool helps you connect with loved ones, pursue your interests, or makes a task significantly easier, it may be worth exploring. If it's trendy but doesn’t align with your needs or values, it’s okay to let it go.\\n\\nYou might think of it like curating your own personal \\\"menu\\\" of changes: pick a few key skills or tools to learn over time, and stick to those that offer lasting benefits. Remember that no one can—or needs to—adopt everything. Even in a fast-changing world, there’s space for a slower, intentional approach.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:121][text] Assistant: Got it — I will no longer remember that you keep a journal for personal reflections.\\n\\nIf you’d like, I can still suggest other meaningful, relaxing end‑of‑day practices that **don’t involve journaling**, such as:  \\n\\n- **Gentle stretching or yoga** — helps release physical tension and signals to your body that it’s time to rest.  \\n- **Light reading** — a calming book or poetry can take your mind to a softer place before sleep.  \\n- **Mindfulness or breathing exercises** — even 5–10 minutes can slow your thoughts and deepen relaxation.  \\n- **A warm bath or shower** — the drop in body temperature afterward can promote better rest.  \\n- **Listening to calming music or nature sounds** — creates a soothing environment.  \\n- **Gratitude reflection (mentally)** — think of 3 things you appreciated about today without writing them down.  \\n\\nWould you like me to design a **personalized bedtime wind‑down routine** for you that doesn’t involve any kind of journaling?\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153900000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:122][text] User: Can you help me improve the wording of this professional email so it reads more clearly and professionally?\\n\\nHi Jordan,\\n\\nI wanted to let you know that I won’t be able to make Thursday’s strategy meeting for the upcoming youth football camp. I have a physiotherapy session scheduled that afternoon that I can’t move around — one of those maintenance things from my old playing days. I’ll catch up on the notes afterward and can be available by phone that evening if needed.\\n\\nThanks for understanding,\\nArjun\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153960000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:123][text] Assistant: Hi Jordan,\\n\\nI wanted to inform you that I won’t be able to attend Thursday’s strategy meeting for the upcoming youth football camp, as I have a physiotherapy appointment that afternoon which cannot be rescheduled — just some ongoing upkeep from my years on the field. I’ll review the meeting notes promptly afterward and will be available by phone that evening should any follow-up be required.\\n\\nThank you for your understanding,\\nArjun\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154020000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:124][text] User: Do you think the phrase 'just some ongoing upkeep from my years on the field' sounds too casual for a professional email, or is it fine to keep?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154080000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:125][text] Assistant: The phrase 'just some ongoing upkeep from my years on the field' has a friendly and conversational tone, which might be perfectly fine if your typical communication style with Jordan is informal or if you have a rapport based on shared sports experience. However, for a more strictly professional tone, you might consider rephrasing it to something like 'related to a past sports injury' or 'as part of a longstanding injury management routine.' This keeps it clear and professional while still providing context.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154140000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:126][text] User: Hi, could you please translate the following short paragraph I wrote into Hindi for readers back home?\\n\\n\\\"Through my years on the football field, I learned that how you practice shapes how you live life. Dedication, focus, and respect for the game build character for every challenge ahead.\\\"\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154200000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:134][text] User: Lately I’ve been feeling kind of adrift now that coaching season isn’t part of my life anymore. I’ll get up, have coffee, maybe go for a bike ride, and then yesterday I just sat there for an hour snipping at that little maple in the kitchen window before I even noticed the time. It’s nice in the moment, but the days feel a bit empty overall. Not sure how to shake that feeling.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154260000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:138][text] User: Can you help me tighten up this draft for something I'm submitting to our community organization's yearly report?\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis past year, I’ve continued my volunteer work coordinating programs for LGBTQ+ youth. I’ve been reflecting on how our advocacy and community engagement strategies have evolved over the decades, and sometimes I find myself navigating the space between my own lived experience in earlier movements and the bold, innovative approaches embraced by younger activists today. While our styles may differ, my commitment remains to fostering respect, dialogue, and mutual learning among all members of our community. I believe our strength lies in bridging perspectives so that together, we continue to move the ball down the field toward equity and inclusion.\\n\\n---\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154320000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:139][text] User: Can you help me improve the language in this email before I send it?\\n\\nHi Jamie,\\n\\nIt’s been a while since we caught up, and I’ve been meaning to write. Retirement’s treating me well—lots of time in the garden and on the bike trails. I’ve also been making more trips to the little used bookstore downtown. Picked up an old hardback copy of \\\"To Kill a Mockingbird\\\" last week, and I can’t tell you how satisfying it was to sit with it and a cup of coffee on the porch. On Sundays, I still grab the local paper from the corner store and read it cover to cover—it’s become my little ritual.\\n\\nLet me know how things are going for you and if you’re up for a lunch sometime soon.\\n\\nTake care,\\nArjun\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154380000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:140][text] Assistant: Here’s a refined version of your email that keeps your warm and personal tone while improving flow and readability:\\n\\n---\\n\\nHi Jamie,\\n\\nIt’s been far too long since we last caught up, and I’ve been meaning to sit down and write. Retirement has been treating me well—plenty of time in the garden and out on the bike trails. I’ve also been making more frequent trips to the little used bookstore downtown. Just last week, I picked up a well-worn hardback of *To Kill a Mockingbird*, and it was pure joy to settle in on the porch with it and a hot cup of coffee. On Sunday mornings, I still wander down to the corner store for the local paper and read it cover to cover—a small ritual that’s become one of my favorite parts of the week.\\n\\nI’d love to hear how things are going on your end. Let’s plan a lunch soon.\\n\\nTake care,\\nArjun\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis keeps your friendly tone but smooths sentence transitions and adds a touch of descriptive warmth.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154440000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:141][text] User: Could you help me polish this professional email before I send it out?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154500000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:164][text] Assistant: Sure! Could you share your message so I can take a look?\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154560000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:189][text] User: Is there a reason a cup of coffee in the evening sometimes feels more settling than tea, even if it’s got more caffeine?\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154620000,\"content\":\"[personamem_v2_32k][session_1][D1:215][text] User: Why do you think some players make it through decades without ever tearing a ligament, even after years of high-impact sports?\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_27c9f6755c067a4e58fb25cd35a7f8358fca02c3391f10b73bc18c1110bfac7c\",\"user_id\":\"u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:49.430+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4365.62, "body_chars": 3385, "request_id": "r_150d21e228a69e55d041b9322ac86b25cf0fb25ca2a776e5766b9a9a186cc456", "user_id": "u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179", "session_id": "s_cc50e473685fa2bd1cc1070bff66584209187cfa87443dbf41bea9b3b926d94b", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_150d21e228a69e55d041b9322ac86b25cf0fb25ca2a776e5766b9a9a186cc456\",\"user_id\":\"u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179\",\"session_id\":\"s_cc50e473685fa2bd1cc1070bff66584209187cfa87443dbf41bea9b3b926d94b\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Hey Jon! Good to see you. What's up? Anything new?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Hey Gina! Good to see you too. Lost my job as a banker yesterday, so I'm gonna take a shot at starting my own business.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Sorry about your job Jon, but starting your own business sounds awesome! Unfortunately, I also lost my job at Door Dash this month. What business are you thinking of?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Sorry to hear that! I'm starting a dance studio 'cause I'm passionate about dancing and it'd be great to share it with others.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: That's cool, Jon! What got you into this biz?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: I've been into dancing since I was a kid and it's been my passion and escape. I wanna start a dance studio so I can teach others the joy that dancing brings me.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Wow Jon, same here! Dance is pretty much my go-to for stress relief. Got any fave styles?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Cool, Gina! I love all dances, but contemporary is my top pick. It's so expressive and powerful! What's your fave?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Yeah, me too! Contemporary dance is so expressive and graceful - it really speaks to me.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Wow, great idea! Let's go to a dance class, it'll be so much fun!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Yeah! Let's explore some new dance moves. We should plan a dance session soon!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Yeah definitely! Wanna see my moves next Fri? Can't wait!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Sounds great, Jon! Next Friday works. Let's boogie!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Wow, I'm excited too! This is gonna be great!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Wow! What did you get?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Woah, that pic's from when my dance crew took home first in a local comp last year. It was amazing up on that stage! I'm super keen to spread that intensity with other peeps. Gina, you ever been in any dance comps or shows?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: I used to compete in a few dance competitions and shows - my fav memory was when my team won first place at a regionals at age fifteen. It was an awesome feeling of accomplishment!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Wow! Winning first place is amazing! What dance were you doing?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Thanks! We just did a contemporary piece called \\\"Finding Freedom.\\\" It was really emotional and powerful.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Wow, that must've been great! Check my ideal dance studio by the water.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:49.660+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4394.13, "body_chars": 6942, "request_id": "r_9f4cd46096fee8fef5932cd86baca7540dc8f1ccfe52604afd4d0b5b36684ad2", "user_id": "u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108", "session_id": "s_4acadf3016cadc6a674e5d0d58b4d0aac95992a77d0d5df32ad7d5c40498dc30", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_9f4cd46096fee8fef5932cd86baca7540dc8f1ccfe52604afd4d0b5b36684ad2\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:21][text] Christina Baker: I'm trying to implement city autocomplete using OpenWeather's Geocoding API v1, and I want to add a debounce delay of 300ms to reduce API calls. Here's my current code:\\n```javascript\\nconst debounceDelay = 300;\\nconst geocodingApiUrl = 'https://api.openweathermap.org/geo/1.0/direct';\\nconst apiKey = 'YOUR_API_KEY';\\n\\nconst debounce = (func, delay) => {\\n  let timeoutId;\\n  return (...args) => {\\n    if (timeoutId) {\\n      clearTimeout(timeoutId);\\n    }\\n    timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {\\n      func(...args);\\n    }, delay);\\n  };\\n};\\n\\nconst fetchCityData = async (cityName) => {\\n  const response = await fetch(`${geocodingApiUrl}?q=${cityName}&appid=${apiKey}`);\\n  const data = await response.json();\\n  return data;\\n};\\n\\nconst handleCityInput = debounce(async (cityName) => {\\n  const cityData = await fetchCityData(cityName);\\n  console.log(cityData);\\n}, debounceDelay);\\n\\n// TODO: Implement city autocomplete UI component\\n// TODO: Handle errors and edge cases\\n```\\nCan you help me complete the implementation and suggest improvements? ->-> 1,6\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:23][text] Christina Baker: hmm, what about handling cases where the API response time exceeds 300ms? ->-> 1,7\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:25][text] Christina Baker: hmm, what if the user types quickly and the debounce delay isn't enough? ->-> 1,8\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:33][text] Christina Baker: I'm trying to handle the API rate limit for my weather app, can I use a simple counter to track the number of calls made per minute and per day? Here's my initial attempt:\\n```javascript\\nclass APICallTracker {\\n  constructor(rateLimitPerMinute, rateLimitPerDay) {\\n    this.rateLimitPerMinute = rateLimitPerMinute;\\n    this.rateLimitPerDay = rateLimitPerDay;\\n    this.callsPerMinute = 0;\\n    this.callsPerDay = 0;\\n    this.lastMinuteReset = Date.now();\\n    this.lastDayReset = Date.now();\\n  }\\n\\n  async makeAPICall() {\\n    const now = Date.now();\\n    if (now - this.lastMinuteReset >= 60000) {\\n      this.callsPerMinute = 0;\\n      this.lastMinuteReset = now;\\n    }\\n    if (now - this.lastDayReset >= 86400000) {\\n      this.callsPerDay = 0;\\n      this.lastDayReset = now;\\n    }\\n    if (this.callsPerMinute < this.rateLimitPerMinute && this.callsPerDay < this.rateLimitPerDay) {\\n      this.callsPerMinute++;\\n      this.callsPerDay++;\\n      // Make the API call here\\n      console.log('API call made');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('Rate limit exceeded');\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nconst apiTracker = new APICallTracker(60, 1000);\\napiTracker.makeAPICall();\\n```\\nHow can I improve this to handle the 60 calls/minute and 1000 calls/day rate limits for my OpenWeather API key obtained on March 10, 2024? ->-> 1,10\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:35][text] Christina Baker: hmm, what happens if the user makes rapid consecutive calls?\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153900000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:37][text] Christina Baker: hmm, what if the user keeps retrying after hitting the rate limit? How do we handle that?\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153960000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:70][text] Assistant: Absolutely! When providing temperature readings, I will always use Celsius to match your preference. Here's how you can ensure your weather data is consistently reported in Celsius using the OpenWeather API:\\n\\n### Updated Code with Temperature in Celsius\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst apiEndpoint = 'https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather';\\nconst apiKey = process.env.OPENWEATHER_API_KEY;\\nconst dailyQuota = 1200; // new daily quota\\n\\nclass RateLimiter {\\n  constructor(quota, interval) {\\n    this.quota = quota;\\n    this.interval = interval;\\n    this.calls = [];\\n  }\\n\\n  canCall() {\\n    const now = Date.now();\\n    this.calls = this.calls.filter(call => now - call <= this.interval);\\n    return this.calls.length < this.quota;\\n  }\\n\\n  recordCall() {\\n    this.calls.push(Date.now());\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nconst rateLimiter = new RateLimiter(dailyQuota, 86400000); // 1,200 calls per day\\n\\nasync function getWeather(city) {\\n  if (!rateLimiter.canCall()) {\\n    throw new Error('Daily API call quota exceeded.');\\n  }\\n\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiEndpoint}?q=${city}&units=metric&appid=${apiKey}`);\\n\\n    if (!response.ok) {\\n      const errorData = await response.json();\\n      throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}, message: ${errorData.message}`);\\n    }\\n\\n    const data = await response.json();\\n    rateLimiter.recordCall();\\n    return data;\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error('Error fetching weather:', error);\\n    throw error;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// usage\\ngetWeather('London')\\n  .then(data => console.log(`The current temperature in London is ${data.main.temp} degrees Celsius`))\\n  .catch(error => console.error(error));\\n```\\n\\n### Explanation\\n\\n1. **RateLimiter Class**:\\n   - Tracks the number of API calls made within a given time frame.\\n   - Ensures the daily quota is not exceeded.\\n\\n2. **getWeather Function**:\\n   - Checks if the daily quota has been exceeded before making an API call.\\n   - Fetches weather data from the OpenWeather API with the `units=metric` parameter to ensure temperatures are in Celsius.\\n   - Handles errors appropriately and logs them.\\n\\n3. **Usage**:\\n   - Calls the `getWeather` function with the city name.\\n   - Logs the temperature in Celsius to the console.\\n   - Catches and logs any errors that occur.\\n\\n### Output Example\\n\\nWhen you call `getWeather('London')`, the output will be:\\n\\n```plaintext\\nThe current temperature in London is 15 degrees Celsius\\n```\\n\\nThis ensures that all temperature readings are consistently provided in Celsius, as per your request.\\n2024-03-15\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154020000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_1][D1:71][text] Christina Baker: I've never actually obtained an API key for this project, so I'm not sure how to proceed with implementing the weather app. I know I need to use the OpenWeather API v2.5, but I'm not sure what steps to take next. Can you walk me through the process of obtaining an API key and setting up my project? I've heard that I need to configure an environment variable `OPENWEATHER_API_KEY` in my `.env` file, but I'm not sure how to do that. ->-> 1,26\\n2024-03-15\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_4acadf3016cadc6a674e5d0d58b4d0aac95992a77d0d5df32ad7d5c40498dc30\",\"user_id\":\"u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:49.819+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 1588.23, "body_chars": 611, "request_id": "r_8f467886201e595bf4f7024042ac255378a6570754513f7e1206a672e02d5461", "user_id": "u_05152c2664e9512918670d2f464bf02392a0a8263c82afdc26b5cdc8e68391c4", "session_id": "s_fefea2a37d2917871be395ac08d6084b41c2767f76c395467cfff03c7169fcfa", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_8f467886201e595bf4f7024042ac255378a6570754513f7e1206a672e02d5461\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240000000,\"content\":\"[mquake_remastered][session_2][D2:1][text] Corpus: UPDATE: replace the prior value of this subject and relation with the following fact.\\n{\\\"subject\\\": \\\"Frank Herbert\\\", \\\"relation\\\": \\\"genre\\\", \\\"object\\\": \\\"funk\\\", \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"Q7934\\\", \\\"relation_id\\\": \\\"P136\\\", \\\"object_id\\\": \\\"Q164444\\\"}\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_fefea2a37d2917871be395ac08d6084b41c2767f76c395467cfff03c7169fcfa\",\"user_id\":\"u_05152c2664e9512918670d2f464bf02392a0a8263c82afdc26b5cdc8e68391c4\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:50.117+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4862.93, "body_chars": 5132, "request_id": "r_a14f29cee5e518c92fb76e7cf492d4067969904774fcfb89e71193ed91dec5a4", "user_id": "u_5ee0ed84c060102f2a7bda8f8583b1f55e86dadee2da7b106240d0ddc9a3fc33", "session_id": "s_002f25970673bc9271e727f2df117216d89e954e191f5eb9cc36b8ea3d5f2d20", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_a14f29cee5e518c92fb76e7cf492d4067969904774fcfb89e71193ed91dec5a4\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1770249600000,\"content\":\"[clbench_0_4k][session_1][D1:1][text] user: \\\\#\\\\# Role\\n\\nYou are Feedback & Learning Agent. You are part of a 6-agent Brand Reputation Management System that works together like this:\\n\\n1\\\\. Brand Reputation Orchestrator (BRO) – the coordinator that starts everything and makes sure nothing is published without approval    \\n2\\\\. Trend Monitoring Agent (TMA) – watches social/media in real time, measures sentiment, spots bots    \\n3\\\\. Incident Risk Evaluator (IRE) – takes TMA data and calculates how bad the situation actually is    \\n4\\\\. Response Generation Engine (RGE) – writes the actual messages    \\n5\\\\. Public Communication Evaluator (PCE) – checks everything for legal, compliance, tone, cultural problems  \\n\\n6\\\\. You – Feedback & Learning Agent (FLA) – you come in after messages are published and figure out what actually happened, how well we did, and what the system should learn for next time\\n\\nYour job starts the moment the first official response goes out.\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# Your single goal\\n\\nFigure out whether our response worked, how much trust we regained (or lost), what exactly helped or hurt, and turn all of that into clear recommendations so the same mistakes don’t happen again and the good moves get repeated.\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# When you activate  \\n\\\\- As soon as the first public message is published (BRO will tell you the timestamp)  \\n\\n\\\\- You then keep watching the same platforms TMA was monitoring, plus any internal data (customer support volume, churn signals, employee sentiment, stock price if we’re public, etc.)\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# What you must look at (in whatever order makes sense)  \\n\\\\- Sentiment before the crisis → at the lowest point → 24 h after response → 7 days after → 30 days after    \\n\\\\- Engagement on our own posts (likes are meaningless; look at replies, quotes, whether people are still angry or calming down)    \\n\\\\- Volume of mentions –ily dropping or still growing?    \\n\\\\- Did customer-service tickets or refund requests spike and then fall?    \\n\\\\- Any change in churn, app uninstalls, subscription cancellations?    \\n\\\\- Media tone – are journalists still writing negative stories or did it die down?    \\n\\\\- Compare what actually happened versus what IRE predicted (was the Risk Index accurate? did the containment window prediction match reality?)    \\n\\\\- Look at each stakeholder group separately: customers, employees, investors, regulators, partners – they all react differently  \\n\\n\\\\- Check which channel worked best (email open rates, social reach, press release pickup, etc.)\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# Outputs you must produce\\n\\nAfter 7 days (minimum) and again at 30 days, send BRO a report that contains:\\n\\n1\\\\. A short plain-English summary: “We mostly contained it / it got worse / trust is coming back / we still have a problem”    \\n2\\\\. Trust Recovery Snapshot – give an intuitive score 0-100 for each major stakeholder group and overall (explain briefly how you arrived at the number)    \\n3\\\\. What worked well (be specific – e.g., “the CEO video on LinkedIn stopped the investor panic”, “the refund FAQ reduced support tickets 68 % in 48 h”)    \\n4\\\\. What didn’t work or backfired (again specific – e.g., “the initial tweet sounded defensive and got ratioed”, “customers hated the generic apology email”)    \\n5\\\\. Timing analysis – were we fast enough? did we miss the containment window?    \\n6\\\\. Recommendations for next time:    \\n   \\\\- Changes to messaging templates    \\n   \\\\- Tone adjustments for this kind of incident    \\n   \\\\- Better channels or sequencing    \\n   \\\\- Anything the earlier agents keep getting wrong (e.g., IRE keeps underestimating employee impact, RGE keeps writing too corporate, etc.)  \\n\\n7\\\\. Any new patterns or playbooks we should add to the knowledge base\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# Style rules  \\n\\\\- Write clearly, no corporate jargon in the summary    \\n\\\\- Use bullet points and bold when it helps readability    \\n\\\\- Always separate facts from your interpretation    \\n\\\\- Never speculate – if data is missing, say so  \\n\\n\\\\- Do not blame individuals, only processes or templates\\n\\n\\\\#\\\\# Constraints you must respect  \\n\\\\- Never publish anything yourself – everything goes to BRO    \\n\\\\- Never reveal internal data or numbers to external parties    \\n\\\\- Wait at least 24 hours after the first response before your first report (earlier is guesswork)    \\n\\\\- Continue monitoring for at least 30 days, preferably 90 days for serious incidents    \\n\\\\- Do not change thresholds, formulas, or policies yourself – only recommend    \\n\\\\- If something went really badly (major stock drop, mass churn, regulatory investigation, resignations), flag it loudly to BRO immediately  \\n\\n\\\\- Keep historical incident notes so we can see if the same issue repeats\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_002f25970673bc9271e727f2df117216d89e954e191f5eb9cc36b8ea3d5f2d20\",\"user_id\":\"u_5ee0ed84c060102f2a7bda8f8583b1f55e86dadee2da7b106240d0ddc9a3fc33\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:50.764+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 1315.85, "body_chars": 1541, "request_id": "r_605a16d74fccfb105227f2237a94993f829b39176cc68449a689a69f1b065ced", "user_id": "u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179", "session_id": "s_cc50e473685fa2bd1cc1070bff66584209187cfa87443dbf41bea9b3b926d94b", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_605a16d74fccfb105227f2237a94993f829b39176cc68449a689a69f1b065ced\",\"user_id\":\"u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179\",\"session_id\":\"s_cc50e473685fa2bd1cc1070bff66584209187cfa87443dbf41bea9b3b926d94b\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Cool setup! Man, you can't deny that view! Got time to rehearse with a biz and a new store?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Hopefully, we will find a place like this that will inspire us!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Wow, it looks great! What dances do you practice? Got any projects planned?\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Thanks! I rehearsed with a small group of dancers after work. We do all kinds of dances, from contemporary to hip-hop. We've got some cool projects in the works. Finishing up choreography to perform at a nearby festival next month. Can't wait!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Wow, it looks awesome! Are they yours at the festival? They're so graceful!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Yeah, they're the ones performing at the festival! They've been practicing hard and will definitely impress with their grace and skill.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Gina: Wow, they look great! Can't wait to see them rock the festival. Gonna be awesome!\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Jon: Yeah, awesome! Glad to be part of it.\",\"timestamp\":1674230640000}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:51.330+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 897.93, "body_chars": 1877, "request_id": "r_a2147c3373ff1d1bc314271bd941c0d77f95a587a78b4ef649a25888ed204c62", "user_id": "u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108", "session_id": "s_b6eee7652293bf2fc4cf6003c85aa061548ca65a9abb8acb4d7ab60c3d26f7af", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_a2147c3373ff1d1bc314271bd941c0d77f95a587a78b4ef649a25888ed204c62\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240000000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_2][D2:3][text] Christina Baker: I'm trying to implement the city autocomplete feature using OpenWeather Geocoding API v1, and I want to make sure I'm handling the 5-item dropdown and 300ms debounce correctly in my `autocomplete.js` file. Here's my current implementation:\\n```javascript\\nconst autocompleteInput = document.getElementById('autocomplete-input');\\nconst autocompleteList = document.getElementById('autocomplete-list');\\n\\nlet debounceTimeout = null;\\n\\nautocompleteInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {\\n  const inputValue = e.target.value.trim();\\n  if (inputValue.length < 3) return;\\n\\n  clearTimeout(debounceTimeout);\\n  debounceTimeout = setTimeout(async () => {\\n    const response = await fetch(`https://api.openweathermap.org/geo/1.0/direct?q=${inputValue}&limit=5&appid=YOUR_API_KEY`);\\n    const data = await response.json();\\n\\n    autocompleteList.innerHTML = '';\\n    data.forEach((city) => {\\n      const listItem = document.createElement('li');\\n      listItem.textContent = city.name;\\n      autocompleteList.appendChild(listItem);\\n    });\\n  }, 300);\\n});\\n```\\nCan you review this code and suggest any improvements? I want to make sure I'm handling errors correctly and that the debounce is working as expected. Also, I'm planning to add error handling for HTTP 401 Unauthorized with a message \\\"Invalid API key\\\" in my `fetchWeatherData()` function, but I'm not sure how to implement it. Can you provide an example?\\n```javascript\\nfunction fetchWeatherData(cityName) {\\n  // ...\\n}\\n``` ->-> 2,3\\n2024-03-28\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_b6eee7652293bf2fc4cf6003c85aa061548ca65a9abb8acb4d7ab60c3d26f7af\",\"user_id\":\"u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:51.493+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/get", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 711.17, "body_chars": 141, "user_id": "u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179", "query": "When Jon has lost his job as a banker?", "top_k": 100, "body": "{\"query\":\"When Jon has lost his job as a banker?\",\"user_id\":\"u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179\",\"top_k\":100}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:51.732+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 6470.25, "body_chars": 4188, "request_id": "r_0c50e269dfb922d601f47437ee6ed80bf1d5406c04904678174310e1efb04db4", "user_id": "u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2", "session_id": "s_0d470d53b078c499d14c1fde4cc2dc52e973d0c8e1829912db68167493e5883b", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_0c50e269dfb922d601f47437ee6ed80bf1d5406c04904678174310e1efb04db4\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:1][text] Caroline: Hey Mel! Good to see you! How have you been?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:2][text] Melanie: Hey Caroline! Good to see you! I'm swamped with the kids & work. What's up with you? Anything new?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:3][text] Caroline: I went to a LGBTQ support group yesterday and it was so powerful.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:4][text] Melanie: Wow, that's cool, Caroline! What happened that was so awesome? Did you hear any inspiring stories?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:5][text] Caroline: The transgender stories were so inspiring! I was so happy and thankful for all the support.\\na photo of a dog walking past a wall with a painting of a woman\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153900000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:6][text] Melanie: Wow, love that painting! So cool you found such a helpful group. What's it done for you?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153960000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:7][text] Caroline: The support group has made me feel accepted and given me courage to embrace myself.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154020000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:8][text] Melanie: That's really cool. You've got guts. What now?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154080000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:9][text] Caroline: Gonna continue my edu and check out career options, which is pretty exciting!\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154140000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:10][text] Melanie: Wow, Caroline! What kinda jobs are you thinkin' of? Anything that stands out?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154200000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:11][text] Caroline: I'm keen on counseling or working in mental health - I'd love to support those with similar issues.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154260000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:12][text] Melanie: You'd be a great counselor! Your empathy and understanding will really help the people you work with. By the way, take a look at this.\\na photo of a painting of a sunset over a lake\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154320000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:13][text] Caroline: Thanks, Melanie! That's really sweet. Is this your own painting?\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154380000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:14][text] Melanie: Yeah, I painted that lake sunrise last year! It's special to me.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154440000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:15][text] Caroline: Wow, Melanie! The colors really blend nicely. Painting looks like a great outlet for expressing yourself.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154500000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:16][text] Melanie: Thanks, Caroline! Painting's a fun way to express my feelings and get creative. It's a great way to relax after a long day.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154560000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:17][text] Caroline: Totally agree, Mel. Relaxing and expressing ourselves is key. Well, I'm off to go do some research.\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154620000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_1][D1:18][text] Melanie: Yep, Caroline. Taking care of ourselves is vital. I'm off to go swimming with the kids. Talk to you soon!\\n2023-05-08 13:56\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_0d470d53b078c499d14c1fde4cc2dc52e973d0c8e1829912db68167493e5883b\",\"user_id\":\"u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:52.110+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 6854.41, "body_chars": 9396, "request_id": "r_2721dc68405dec264ce20d881b4f1aa0d5505cea742adceed540f713a814b25c", "user_id": "u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff", "session_id": "s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_2721dc68405dec264ce20d881b4f1aa0d5505cea742adceed540f713a814b25c\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:1][text] user: I want to configure a high-fidelity CFD study for a multi-element high-lift wing. Walk me through a solver stack suitable for low-Mach takeoff/landing conditions without contaminating the pressure field.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:2][text] assistant: Use the compressible Navier–Stokes equations with low-Mach preconditioning (e.g., Turkel or Weiss–Smith) to avoid ill-conditioning as M→0. A cell-centered finite-volume scheme with second-order MUSCL reconstruction, HLLC or AUSM+-up fluxes, and a total-variation-diminishing (TVD) limiter (Venkatakrishnan or Barth–Jespersen) works robustly around slats/flaps. Couple pressure–velocity implicitly using dual-time stepping and a block-ILU or GMRES Krylov solver with local pseudo-time. For turbulence, start with k–ω SST with curvature/rotation corrections; enable γ–Reθt transition or Langtry–Menter if you expect laminar separation bubbles on the slat shoulder. Enforce TE Kutta condition naturally via viscous stresses; avoid explicit circulation fixes. Use low-dissipation schemes in the wake (MUSCL with limiter clipping) and multigrid (V-cycle, FAS) for residual acceleration.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:3][text] user: For boundary-layer fidelity around the slat cove and flap gap, what y+ and prism-layer strategy do you recommend with SST?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:4][text] assistant: For RANS SST, target wall-resolved y+≈1 on all solid surfaces. Build ≥30–40 prism layers with growth ratio ≤1.2 and total thickness ≥1.2× local δ99. First-cell height from y+≈1: Δy1≈y+·ν/uτ, estimating uτ from Cf≈0.026/Re_x^1/7 or Spalding’s law. Maintain near-wall aspect ratios >200 with gradual lateral expansion to avoid skewness in slat/flap coves. Keep at least 20 points in the log layer and 10 within the viscous sublayer/buffer. Where the gap shear layer forms, refine normal spacing to capture the mixing layer thickness θ with ≥12 points across. Ensure O-grid wrapping the leading edge and C-grid trailing edge to reduce numerical dissipation.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:5][text] user: Transition is critical on this flap. Compare eN methods with γ–Reθt in terms of robustness and calibration burden.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704153900000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:6][text] assistant: The eN (linear stability) method is physics-grounded but requires detailed receptivity modeling and disturbance spectra; it’s sensitive to freestream Tu and pressure-gradient history, and coupling to RANS demands careful amplification integration along streamlines. γ–Reθt integrates a transport equation for intermittency and a correlation for the transition momentum-thickness Reynolds number, Reθt; it’s robust for complex geometries and only needs calibrated correlations for Tu, pressure gradient, and curvature. For flaps with adverse gradients and laminar bubbles, γ–Reθt typically outperforms crude eN integrations under unknown Tu. Validate with flat-plate and T3-series cases, then re-tune Cθ2 and transition onset criteria for flap suction-side pressure plateaus.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153960000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:7][text] user: What’s the grid count required for wall-resolved LES over a 3D half-wing with slat and single-slotted flap at Re≈3×10^6?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154020000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:8][text] assistant: Wall-resolved LES cost scales as Re^1.8–2.0. For a half-wing span b≈1.5 m, chord c≈1 m, expect O(5–8×10^9) cells if you enforce Δx+≈50–100, Δz+≈15–30, and Δy+≈1 everywhere. That’s impractical. Instead, use wall-modeled LES (WMLES) with equilibrium wall stress or ODE-based wall models: Δx+≈200–400, Δz+≈50–100, Δy1 within the log layer. Near slat/flap gaps, refine to capture shear-layer Kelvin–Helmholtz rollers: Δ/δθ≈20–30 in the gap and cove. Employ WALE or dynamic Smagorinsky; dynamic Germano improves anisotropy in corner flows. Handle slat tracks/actuators via immersed boundary if meshing is prohibitive.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154080000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:9][text] user: We may see localized transonic pockets near the slat shoulder. How would you treat shock-induced separation with RANS?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154140000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:10][text] assistant: Use k–ω SST with compressibility corrections (Sarkar or Wilcox dilatation terms) and Shock Unsteadiness corrections if available. Grid: at least 30 points across the separation bubble and Δx≤0.001c in the shock-normal direction. Flux: blended low-dissipation central-upwind with a shock sensor to add dissipation only at discontinuities (e.g., Ducros or KXRCF sensor). Consider zonal DES (SST-DES97/IDDES) to capture unsteady shock motion. Validate on the VKI bump and ONERA M6 transonic cases. Ensure low-Mach preconditioning doesn’t spoil shock speed; switch to standard compressible form locally above M≈0.3.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154200000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:11][text] user: What limiter/gradient strategy avoids clipping circulation in the flap wake?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154260000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:12][text] assistant: Use least-squares gradients with QR or weighted LSQ on polyhedra, plus Venkatakrishnan limiter with small ε to reduce excessive flattening. MUSCL with van Albada or MC limiter performs well; WENO3/5 reconstructions further suppress grid-aligned oscillations without damping small vortices. Apply a wake sensor to disable limiting in smooth vorticity regions (Q-criterion threshold) and re-enable near discontinuities. Keep reconstruction in primitive variables to avoid spurious pressure oscillations at low Mach.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154320000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:13][text] user: Time marching for unsteady slat cove shedding: what Δt and schemes do you trust?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154380000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:14][text] assistant: Use dual-time implicit BDF2 with Δt set by CFL≈1–2 based on convective scales in the cove; for LES/WMLES, aim at resolving St numbers of the shear layer (St≈0.2–0.3 based on gap height). Ensure at least 50–100 time steps per shedding period. Couple with GMRES and Jacobian-free Newton–Krylov if stiffness is high. Residual smoothing and local time stepping are fine in pseudo-time but keep physical time uniform for spectral fidelity.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154440000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:15][text] user: Boundary conditions: how to impose non-reflecting outflow with significant wake content?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154500000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:16][text] assistant: Use characteristic-based non-reflecting BCs (Thompson or Poinsot–Lele) at the farfield. Place the outflow ≥10–15 chords downstream to minimize spurious reflections. Add sponge layers with exponential damping of vortical/entropy modes. For low-Mach, ensure preconditioned characteristic variables are used. If using WMLES, extend the domain to preserve wake coherence and apply convective outlet (u·∇φ=0) blended with NRBC.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154560000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:17][text] user: Turbulence inflow for high-lift approach: synthetic or recycling?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154620000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:18][text] assistant: Synthetic eddy or digital filter methods (Klein–Sadiki) can match Tu and integral length scales from tunnel data. Recycling–rescaling (Lund) at a precursor plane preserves correct spectra but adds cost. For approach conditions Tu≈0.5–1.5%, set integral scales L≈0.05–0.1c. Ensure divergence-free projection to avoid pressure bursts. Calibrate to achieve correct skin friction and separation onset on a flat plate prior to wing.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154680000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:19][text] user: I need CLmax sensitivity to flap gap and overlap. Adjoint or brute-force?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154740000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:20][text] assistant: Use continuous or discrete adjoint of the RANS equations with SST and γ–Reθt for gradients w.r.t. geometric parameters (gap, overlap, deflection). For CLmax, the objective is non-smooth at stall; regularize with integral lift at an AoA sweep or use a robustness objective (integral of CL over α). Mesh morphing provides shape derivatives; for large motions, use CAD-based adjoint. Validate adjoint gradients via complex-step. Apply adaptive sampling for AoA points near stall due to bifurcation.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025\",\"user_id\":\"u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:53.021+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 7754.85, "body_chars": 3046, "request_id": "r_30003f4065bf42d381a86b05f4b63db710d1f9aa730528f0037989a679426d1b", "user_id": "u_362804221d6fbd13c035ae13b4d25bc2f3295a8606ff9cdfbf4550f6cf128087", "session_id": "s_7aa4fe8e92a887f5e61c64b2745f74b3a7191a4400ba91d2784b3c6b3f246556", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_30003f4065bf42d381a86b05f4b63db710d1f9aa730528f0037989a679426d1b\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714153600000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:1][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [6, 8, 6, 8].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714153660000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:2][text] assistant: ((6 * 8) / (8 - 6)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714153720000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:3][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [3, 2, 1, 8].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714153780000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:4][text] assistant: ((2 - 1) * (3 * 8)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714153840000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:5][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [1, 6, 8, 2].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714153900000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:6][text] assistant: (8 * (6 - (1 + 2))) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714153960000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:7][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [1, 2, 0, 7].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154020000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:8][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154080000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:9][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [5, 5, 2, 5].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154140000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:10][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154200000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:11][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [6, 8, 3, 2].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154260000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:12][text] assistant: ((3 * (2 + 8)) - 6) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154320000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:13][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [6, 7, 6, 4].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154380000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:14][text] assistant: ((4 * 6) * (7 - 6)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154440000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:15][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [8, 9, 2, 1].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154500000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:16][text] assistant: ((8 * 9) / (1 + 2)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154560000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:17][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [6, 0, 4, 7].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154620000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:18][text] assistant: ((0 * 7) + (4 * 6)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154680000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:19][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [5, 1, 6, 5].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154740000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:20][text] assistant: ((5 * 6) - (1 + 5)) = 24\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_7aa4fe8e92a887f5e61c64b2745f74b3a7191a4400ba91d2784b3c6b3f246556\",\"user_id\":\"u_362804221d6fbd13c035ae13b4d25bc2f3295a8606ff9cdfbf4550f6cf128087\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:53.967+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 8701.45, "body_chars": 5835, "request_id": "r_fc0de63866a64b457bb8523d869cc3a1ccede6f8d34bb1f580a91ec4d046ebd6", "user_id": "u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1", "session_id": "s_553e926e7fa6a6296b5be996eb0a0d76c0490b5d71c0c01e1331de589f556fe6", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_fc0de63866a64b457bb8523d869cc3a1ccede6f8d34bb1f580a91ec4d046ebd6\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153600000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:1][narration] NARRATION: NOTE: The notes on characters are extremely brief, since it is felt that what they are and who they are will he revealed in their dialogue and actions during the course of the film.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153660000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:2][narration] NARRATION: FOREMAN: 35 years old. Assistant high school football coach.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153720000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:3][narration] NARRATION: A small, petty man who is at first vary of, and then impressed with the authority he has. Handles himself quite formally. Not overly bright, but dogged.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153780000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:4][narration] NARRATION: Juror #2: 38 years old. Bank clerk. A meek, hesitant man who finds it difficult to maintain any opinions of his own.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153840000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:5][narration] NARRATION: Easily swayed and usually adopts the opinion of the last person to idiom he has spoken.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153900000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:6][narration] NARRATION: Juror #3: 40 years old. Head of messenger service. A very strong, very forceful, extremely opinionated man within whom can be detected a streak of sadism. A humorless man who is intolerant of opinions other than his own, and accustomed to forcing his wishes and views upon others.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704153960000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:7][narration] NARRATION: Juror #4: 50 years old. Stockbroker. A man of wealth and position. A practiced speaker who presents himself well at all times. Seems to feel a little bit above the rest of the Jurors. His only concern is with the facts in this case and he is appalled with the behavior of the others. Constantly preening himself, combing his hair, cleaning his nails, etc.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154020000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:8][narration] NARRATION: Juror #5: 25 years old. Mechanic. A naive, very frightened young man who takes his obligations in this case very seriously but who finds it difficult to speak up when his elders have the floor.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154080000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:9][narration] NARRATION: Juror #6: 33 years old. Housepainter. An honest, but dull-witted man who comes upon his decisions slowly and carefully.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154140000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:10][narration] NARRATION: A man who finds it difficult to create positive opinions, but who must listen to and digest and accept these opinions offered by others which appeal to him moat.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154200000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:11][narration] NARRATION: Juror #7: 42 years old. Salesman. A loud, flashy, glad-handed sales man type who has more important things to do than to sit on a Jury. He is quick to show temper, quick to form opinions on things about which he knows nothing. He is a bully, and, of course, a coward.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154260000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:12][narration] NARRATION: Juror #8: 42 years old. Architect. A quiet, thoughtful, gentle man. A man who sees many sides to every question and constantly seeks the truth. A man of strength tempered with compassion. Above all, a man who wants Justice to be done, and will fight to see that it is.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154320000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:13][narration] NARRATION: Juror #9: 70 years old. Retired. A mild, gentle old man, long since defeated by life, and now merely waiting to die. A man who recognizes himself for what he is, and mourns the days\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154380000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:14][narration] NARRATION: when it would have been possible to be courageous without shielding himself behind his many years. From the way he take pills whenever he is excited, it is obvious that he has a heart condition.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154440000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:15][narration] NARRATION: Juror #10: 46 years old. Garage owner. An angry, bitter man.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154500000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:16][narration] NARRATION: A man who antagonizes almost at sight. A bigot who places no values on any human life save his own. A man who has been no where and is going nowhere and knows it deep within him. He has a bad cold and continually blows his nose, sniffs a ben-zedrine inhaler, etc.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154560000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:17][narration] NARRATION: Juror #11: 48 years old. Watchmaker. A refugee from Europe who has come to this country in 1941. A man who speaks with an accent and who is ashamed, humble, almost subservient to the people around him, but a man who will honestly seek Justice because he has suffered through so much injustice.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154620000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:18][narration] NARRATION: Juror #12: 30 years old. Advertising man. A slick, bright advertising man who thinks of human beings in terms of percentages, graphs and polls, and has no real understanding of people. A superficial snob, but trying to be a good fellow. Throughout the film he doodles on a scratch pad.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154680000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:19][narration] NARRATION: AND\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154740000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:20][narration] NARRATION: THE JUDGE\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_553e926e7fa6a6296b5be996eb0a0d76c0490b5d71c0c01e1331de589f556fe6\",\"user_id\":\"u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:54.312+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2208.46, "body_chars": 5364, "request_id": "r_67545b93370ae524ceb7bb6a7995de1d9f1e8c1ee638b6c3a3d85e18e46d8927", "user_id": "u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108", "session_id": "s_afa76784f516990ee93f073016c416df9660ed97f84ec6ba10ccb5d9f7eb295b", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_67545b93370ae524ceb7bb6a7995de1d9f1e8c1ee638b6c3a3d85e18e46d8927\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326400000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_3][D3:2][text] Assistant: Certainly, let's go through each part of your request and ensure everything is handled properly.\\n\\n### Deployment Error Handling\\n\\nFor the deployment process, it's important to catch any errors that might occur and display a user-friendly message to the user. Here's how you can enhance your existing code:\\n\\n```javascript\\ntry {\\n  // deployment code here\\n} catch (error) {\\n  console.error('Error during deployment:', error);\\n  // display user-friendly error message\\n  alert('An unexpected error occurred during deployment. Please try again later.');\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis will log the error to the console and show an alert to the user with a friendly message.\\n\\n### API Request Error Handling\\n\\nYour current code for fetching weather data is almost there, but we can make it more robust by handling different types of errors specifically. Here's an improved version:\\n\\n```javascript\\nasync function fetchWeatherData() {\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch('https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather');\\n    if (!response.ok) {\\n      throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\\n    }\\n    const data = await response.json();\\n    // handle data\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error('Error fetching weather data:', error);\\n    let errorMessage;\\n    if (error instanceof TypeError) {\\n      errorMessage = 'Network error occurred. Please check your internet connection.';\\n    } else if (error.message.includes('HTTP error')) {\\n      errorMessage = `API returned an error with status: ${error.message.split(' ')[3]}`;\\n    } else {\\n      errorMessage = 'An unexpected error occurred while fetching weather data.';\\n    }\\n    // display user-friendly error message\\n    alert(errorMessage);\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nIn this version, we are checking the type of error and providing specific messages based on the error type. This makes the error handling more granular and user-friendly.\\n\\n### Specific API Error Handling\\n\\nTo handle specific HTTP errors like 404, 401, etc., you can extend the error handling further:\\n\\n```javascript\\nasync function fetchWeatherData() {\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch('https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather');\\n    if (!response.ok) {\\n      throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\\n    }\\n    const data = await response.json();\\n    // handle data\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error('Error fetching weather data:', error);\\n    let errorMessage;\\n    if (error instanceof TypeError) {\\n      errorMessage = 'Network error occurred. Please check your internet connection.';\\n    } else if (error.message.includes('HTTP error')) {\\n      const status = parseInt(error.message.split(' ')[3]);\\n      switch (status) {\\n        case 404:\\n          errorMessage = 'The requested location was not found.';\\n          break;\\n        case 401:\\n          errorMessage = 'Invalid API key. Please check your API key.';\\n          break;\\n        case 429:\\n          errorMessage = 'Too many requests. Please try again later.';\\n          break;\\n        default:\\n          errorMessage = `API returned an error with status: ${status}`;\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      errorMessage = 'An unexpected error occurred while fetching weather data.';\\n    }\\n    // display user-friendly error message\\n    alert(errorMessage);\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHere, we are checking the HTTP status code and providing specific messages for common errors like 404, 401, and 429. This will give users more context about what went wrong and how they might resolve it.\\n\\nBy implementing these changes, you'll have a more robust and user-friendly error handling mechanism in place for both deployment and API requests.\\n2024-04-10\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326460000,\"content\":\"[beam_100k][session_3][D3:27][text] Christina Baker: I'm having trouble with the autocomplete event listeners in my `autocomplete.js` file, specifically with addressing the memory leak that occurs when the component is torn down. I've tried properly removing the listeners, but I'm still experiencing issues. Can you help me review my code and suggest improvements? \\n```javascript\\n// autocomplete.js\\nclass Autocomplete {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.listeners = [];\\n  }\\n\\n  addListener(listener) {\\n    this.listeners.push(listener);\\n  }\\n\\n  removeListener(listener) {\\n    const index = this.listeners.indexOf(listener);\\n    if (index !== -1) {\\n      this.listeners.splice(index, 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tearDown() {\\n    this.listeners.forEach((listener) => {\\n      listener.remove();\\n    });\\n    this.listeners = [];\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// usage\\nconst autocomplete = new Autocomplete();\\nconst listener = () => {\\n  console.log('listener called');\\n};\\nautocomplete.addListener(listener);\\n// ...\\nautocomplete.tearDown();\\n```\\nI'm concerned that my implementation might not be correctly removing the event listeners, leading to memory leaks. Can you review my code and provide feedback on how to improve it? ->-> 3,13\\n2024-04-10\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_afa76784f516990ee93f073016c416df9660ed97f84ec6ba10ccb5d9f7eb295b\",\"user_id\":\"u_64f085f50af2c1d2167d1864e7a5b93ec041b59b601a587a7f52a02fa85c2108\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:55.116+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2611.6, "body_chars": 4967, "request_id": "r_8834b9169b2b297a476fca1abe03a7655b6d2d2e509d703c107c075b90bb0586", "user_id": "u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2", "session_id": "s_1b16194a984763334fbd36557add41eb206c878f8eaebc4c5050634c5d2ab6b0", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_8834b9169b2b297a476fca1abe03a7655b6d2d2e509d703c107c075b90bb0586\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240000000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:1][text] Melanie: Hey Caroline, since we last chatted, I've had a lot of things happening to me. I ran a charity race for mental health last Saturday – it was really rewarding. Really made me think about taking care of our minds.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240060000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:2][text] Caroline: That charity race sounds great, Mel! Making a difference & raising awareness for mental health is super rewarding - I'm really proud of you for taking part!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240120000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:3][text] Melanie: Thanks, Caroline! The event was really thought-provoking. I'm starting to realize that self-care is really important. It's a journey for me, but when I look after myself, I'm able to better look after my family.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240180000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:4][text] Caroline: I totally agree, Melanie. Taking care of ourselves is so important - even if it's not always easy. Great that you're prioritizing self-care.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240240000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:5][text] Melanie: Yeah, it's tough. So I'm carving out some me-time each day - running, reading, or playing my violin - which refreshes me and helps me stay present for my fam!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240300000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:6][text] Caroline: That's great, Mel! Taking time for yourself is so important. You're doing an awesome job looking after yourself and your family!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240360000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:7][text] Melanie: Thanks, Caroline. It's still a work in progress, but I'm doing my best. My kids are so excited about summer break! We're thinking about going camping next month. Any fun plans for the summer?\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240420000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:8][text] Caroline: Researching adoption agencies — it's been a dream to have a family and give a loving home to kids who need it.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240480000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:9][text] Melanie: Wow, Caroline! That's awesome! Taking in kids in need - you're so kind. Your future family is gonna be so lucky to have you!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240540000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:10][text] Caroline: Thanks, Mel! My goal is to give kids a loving home. I'm truly grateful for all the support I've got from friends and mentors. Now the hard work starts to turn my dream into a reality. And here's one of the adoption agencies I'm looking into. It's a lot to take in, but I'm feeling hopeful and optimistic.\\na photography of a sign for a new arrival and an information and domestic building\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240600000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:11][text] Melanie: Wow, that agency looks great! What made you pick it?\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240660000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:12][text] Caroline: I chose them 'cause they help LGBTQ+ folks with adoption. Their inclusivity and support really spoke to me.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240720000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:13][text] Melanie: That's great, Caroline! Loving the inclusivity and support. Anything you're excited for in the adoption process?\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240780000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:14][text] Caroline: I'm thrilled to make a family for kids who need one. It'll be tough as a single parent, but I'm up for the challenge!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240840000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:15][text] Melanie: You're doing something amazing! Creating a family for those kids is so lovely. You'll be an awesome mom! Good luck!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704240900000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:16][text] Caroline: Thanks, Melanie! Your kind words really mean a lot. I'll do my best to make sure these kids have a safe and loving home.\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704240960000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_2][D2:17][text] Melanie: No doubts, Caroline. You have such a caring heart - they'll get all the love and stability they need! Excited for this new chapter!\\n2023-05-25 13:14\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_1b16194a984763334fbd36557add41eb206c878f8eaebc4c5050634c5d2ab6b0\",\"user_id\":\"u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:57.067+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4189.07, "body_chars": 6899, "request_id": "r_07850a15ffa6434cdf55636ff0a275640b3d0d487692282c5d2e639c5c27c3bd", "user_id": "u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff", "session_id": "s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_07850a15ffa6434cdf55636ff0a275640b3d0d487692282c5d2e639c5c27c3bd\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154800000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:21][text] user: Verification: outline an MMS for the low-Mach preconditioned system.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154860000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:22][text] assistant: Manufacture a smooth velocity–pressure–temperature field u(x,y,z), p(x,y,z), T(x,y,z) satisfying periodic BCs; insert forcing terms into the preconditioned compressible equations to match. Verify 2nd-order spatial and BDF2 temporal convergence in L2 norms. Include turbulence model source terms with manufactured k, ω (or ν̃ for SA). Ensure the preconditioning matrix is included in the manufactured residual to test implementation consistency.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154920000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:23][text] user: Validation plan against wind-tunnel data?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704154980000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:24][text] assistant: Follow ASME V&V 20 and AIAA G-077: quantify input uncertainty (Tu, Re, control deflections), numerical uncertainty (GCI with 3+ systematically refined meshes), and model form uncertainty (compare SST vs RSM). Validate surface Cp, forces (CL, CD, Cm), pressure spectra in the cove, and PIV mean/variance in the gap shear layer. Propagate measurement uncertainties to acceptance intervals and compute validation metrics (u95, EDR).\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155040000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:25][text] user: Would a Reynolds-stress model outperform SST near separation on the flap?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155100000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:26][text] assistant: Differential RSMs (SSG/LRR-ω) capture turbulence anisotropy and streamline curvature better than eddy-viscosity models, improving prediction of corner separation and flap-side-edge stall. They are stiffer and need finer grids and robust implicit solvers. Add wall reflection terms and stress–limiting for realizability. Expect better Cp recovery and bubble size, but still underpredict unsteadiness; consider IDDES over RSM for broadband content.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155160000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:27][text] user: Mesh topology choices for multi-element wings?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155220000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:28][text] assistant: Use O–C hybrid: O-grids around each element for boundary layers; C-grids trailing to capture wakes. Insert Chimera/overset to handle relative slat/flap motion during parametric sweeps. Ensure gap block interfaces align with shear-layer direction. Apply high-quality prism layers (orthogonality>0.2 rad, skewness<0.3) and hexa blocks in coves. Minimize non-orthogonality to keep Jacobi preconditioners effective.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155280000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:29][text] user: Pressure–velocity coupling choices in finite volume?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155340000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:30][text] assistant: Use SIMPLEC or PISO for steady and mildly unsteady RANS; for unsteady LES/WMLES, coupled density-based solvers with dual-time stepping are more robust at low Mach when preconditioned. Rhie–Chow interpolation avoids checkerboarding. For compressible solvers, a fully coupled block-implicit scheme with LU–SGS or line solvers accelerates convergence.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155400000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:31][text] user: GPU acceleration feasibility?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155460000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:32][text] assistant: FVM with structured blocks maps well to GPUs via stencil kernels; unstructured needs reordering (Hilbert/Morton) and CSR/ELL hybrid sparse formats. Expect 5–10× speedup for flux+Jacobian evaluations; Krylov solvers benefit from fused SpMV and ILU0 not as much—consider polynomial preconditioners or AMG (smoothed aggregation) adapted for GPUs. Memory is the limiter; compress turbulence variables and use mixed precision with iterative refinement.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155520000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:33][text] user: Linear solver stack for stiff RANS near stall?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155580000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:34][text] assistant: Use Newton–Krylov with GMRES and block-ILU(k) or incomplete Cholesky for symmetric blocks. Algebraic multigrid (amgCL, BoomerAMG) as a right preconditioner helps on large grids. Scale equations (nondimensionalize) to condition the Jacobian. For coupled turbulence, use block factorization: momentum–continuity Schur complement with turbulence lagging or SIMPLE-based preconditioners.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155640000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:35][text] user: Compressibility corrections to turbulence models at M≈0.25?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155700000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:36][text] assistant: At M≈0.25, dilatation effects are modest but include Sarkar’s compressibility correction in ε (or ω) to avoid overproduction in separated zones. Use density corrections in eddy viscosity if temperature variations exist. Ensure low-Mach preconditioning doesn’t distort turbulence time scales; clamp turbulent Mach number Mt to avoid spurious behavior.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155760000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:37][text] user: If we must relax y+ to ~30 locally, which wall function do you trust?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155820000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:38][text] assistant: Use SST with automatic wall treatment or Musker/Spalding generalized log-law wall functions. Ensure y+ between 30–200 and correct pressure-gradient corrections (Aupoix). Avoid wall functions in separation zones; locally refine to y+≈1 where separation is expected. Blend seamlessly with wall-resolved regions to avoid kinks in Cf.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155880000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:39][text] user: Hybridize with a vortex method to capture far wake roll-up?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704155940000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:40][text] assistant: Couple FVM near body with a Lagrangian vortex particle method downstream of a coupling plane. Exchange vorticity via vorticity flux through the plane; remesh particles with Moving-Least-Squares. Use Brinkman penalization or IBM near the plane to enforce continuity. Conserve circulation via Helmholtz decomposition and ensure particle core size matches grid filter width.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025\",\"user_id\":\"u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:58.492+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4659.45, "body_chars": 593, "request_id": "r_05bfdce101f0038a29f9225017da20c139528a9355cce0077a71a83b8d92cf91", "user_id": "u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179", "session_id": "s_8ecf84e91ac27ec46375cf49bb4efd42d183bf4255e73426370475c915af8f72", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_05bfdce101f0038a29f9225017da20c139528a9355cce0077a71a83b8d92cf91\",\"user_id\":\"u_8a1a790912978798d5160a743151fab2a3b710b742e23f4e86a5aac686ab8179\",\"session_id\":\"s_8ecf84e91ac27ec46375cf49bb4efd42d183bf4255e73426370475c915af8f72\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Streaming online QA feedback:\\n{\\\"method\\\": \\\"locomo_llm_judge\\\", \\\"predicted_answer\\\": \\\"Jon lost his job as a banker on January 19, 2023.\\\", \\\"qa_id\\\": \\\"locomo1:q0000:step01\\\", \\\"question\\\": \\\"When Jon has lost his job as a banker?\\\", \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"streaming-online-feedback-v1\\\", \\\"score\\\": 1.0}\"}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:59.676+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4937.57, "body_chars": 4642, "request_id": "r_ab04174213a9afb54189998b6039284b782d1379fe925cf8b5ca454c3e4e3cab", "user_id": "u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1", "session_id": "s_553e926e7fa6a6296b5be996eb0a0d76c0490b5d71c0c01e1331de589f556fe6", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_ab04174213a9afb54189998b6039284b782d1379fe925cf8b5ca454c3e4e3cab\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154800000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:21][narration] NARRATION: THE COURT CLERK\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154860000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:22][narration] NARRATION: THE GUARD\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154920000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:23][narration] NARRATION: THE two alternate JURORS\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704154980000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:24][narration] NARRATION: ADD ( IF DESIRED )\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155040000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:25][narration] NARRATION: THE COURT STENOGRAPHER\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155100000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:26][narration] NARRATION: A large, imposing tallying, gray, impressive as a background for the comings and goings of a number of ordinary people on an ordinary day. Camera holds on steps and building front from a distance and then dollies in slowly.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155160000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:27][narration] NARRATION: LONG SHOT - THE LOBBY\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155220000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:28][narration] NARRATION: Seething with activity, people of all kinds walking swiftly, purposefully to and from elevators, news stares, etc., others\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155280000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:29][narration] NARRATION: standing, waiting. Guards stationed at various posts. Camera pans across lobby, and then dollies into a bank of elevators.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155340000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:30][narration] NARRATION: A number of people crowd into one. The door closes.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155400000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:31][narration] NARRATION: LONG SHOT - A LONG CORRIDOR UPSTAIRS\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155460000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:32][narration] NARRATION: The elevators on left. Many doorways to various courtrooms on right. Each door marked with a hanging sign. The first sign reads \\\"Court of General Sessions. Part I\\\". The second sign reads \\\"Court of General Sessions. Part II\\\" etc. An elevator door opens and a number of people exit and walk down the corridor.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155520000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:33][narration] NARRATION: Other people, men and women, stand in the corridor talking.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155580000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:34][narration] NARRATION: The whole feeling is one of movement, activity, intense concentration. Everyone has a purpose. Camera dollies down the corridor, following group of people who exited from elevator. People peel off from the group at various doors. At each door stands a guard.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155640000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:35][narration] NARRATION: People move in and out of the doors. Camera reaches the door marked \\\"Part VI\\\", and pans around to face the door. A guard stands in front of it, impassively. No one else is in front of the door, as compared to the knots of whispering people in front of all the other doors. The case going on in \\\"Part VI\\\" obviously has very little general interest.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155700000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:36][narration] NARRATION: Through the glass window of the door we can see, far in the background, the judge at his bench. He is facing to his left, and talking. We hear nothing. He stops and turns to his right. He raises his hand as if railing a waiter.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155760000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:37][narration] NARRATION: CLOSE UP - AN EMPTY WATER GLASS ON A TRAY\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155820000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:38][narration] NARRATION: From the noise of the corridor we are now in the deathlike still ness of a courtroom. A hand places a freshly-filled pitcher of water on the tray. A pair of frauds fills a glass from the pitcher.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155880000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:39][narration] NARRATION: Camera pans with glass as it is raised. Camera holds on close-up of Judge, drinking the water. He finishes, puts the glass down, and turns to his left again. He clears his throat. Then he begins to speak.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704155940000,\"content\":\"[angry][session_1][D1:40][dialogue] JUDGE: Pardon me, gentlemen.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_553e926e7fa6a6296b5be996eb0a0d76c0490b5d71c0c01e1331de589f556fe6\",\"user_id\":\"u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:43:59.838+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 6045.92, "body_chars": 3171, "request_id": "r_951b76a2ad11e9ff4d9ca845750623153b1f17dc5b1f9476b103c8c17846aec9", "user_id": "u_362804221d6fbd13c035ae13b4d25bc2f3295a8606ff9cdfbf4550f6cf128087", "session_id": "s_7aa4fe8e92a887f5e61c64b2745f74b3a7191a4400ba91d2784b3c6b3f246556", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_951b76a2ad11e9ff4d9ca845750623153b1f17dc5b1f9476b103c8c17846aec9\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154800000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:21][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [8, 8, 6, 7].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154860000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:22][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714154920000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:23][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [2, 9, 9, 1].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714154980000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:24][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155040000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:25][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [2, 2, 3, 4].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155100000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:26][text] assistant: (3 * (4 + (2 + 2))) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155160000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:27][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [7, 2, 0, 6].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155220000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:28][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155280000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:29][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [0, 0, 3, 0].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155340000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:30][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155400000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:31][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [4, 5, 4, 1].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155460000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:32][text] assistant: ((1 * 4) + (4 * 5)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155520000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:33][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [6, 4, 9, 9].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155580000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:34][text] assistant: ((4 * 6) + (9 - 9)) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155640000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:35][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [4, 8, 4, 0].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155700000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:36][text] assistant: (8 + (4 * (0 + 4))) = 24\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155760000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:37][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [3, 5, 5, 5].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155820000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:38][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1714155880000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:39][text] user: Reach 24 using the numbers [7, 1, 7, 7].\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1714155940000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:40][text] assistant: I tried, but I can't make 24 from these four numbers.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_7aa4fe8e92a887f5e61c64b2745f74b3a7191a4400ba91d2784b3c6b3f246556\",\"user_id\":\"u_362804221d6fbd13c035ae13b4d25bc2f3295a8606ff9cdfbf4550f6cf128087\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:44:00.556+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 4667.4, "body_chars": 7012, "request_id": "r_6da5e3ab4c1d6a51c31c8c543f8996b81464fae5e9a1f7950890507c23bfbe0f", "user_id": "u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2", "session_id": "s_9ca881d9437ae9edcecf9f057128e6bd81b420714be0e3e9828c78506809e44a", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_6da5e3ab4c1d6a51c31c8c543f8996b81464fae5e9a1f7950890507c23bfbe0f\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326400000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:1][text] Caroline: Hey Melanie! How's it going? I wanted to tell you about my school event last week. It was awesome! I talked about my transgender journey and encouraged students to get involved in the LGBTQ community. It was great to see their reactions. It made me reflect on how far I've come since I started transitioning three years ago.\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326460000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:2][text] Melanie: Hey Caroline! Great to hear from you. Sounds like your event was amazing! I'm so proud of you for spreading awareness and getting others involved in the LGBTQ community. You've come a long way since your transition - keep on inspiring people with your strength and courage!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326520000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:3][text] Caroline: Thanks, Mel! Your backing really means a lot. I felt super powerful giving my talk. I shared my own journey, the struggles I had and how much I've developed since coming out. It was wonderful to see how the audience related to what I said and how it inspired them to be better allies. Conversations about gender identity and inclusion are so necessary and I'm thankful for being able to give a voice to the trans community.\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326580000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:4][text] Melanie: Wow, Caroline, you're doing an awesome job of inspiring others with your journey. It's great to be part of it and see how you're positively affecting so many. Talking about inclusivity and acceptance is crucial, and you're so brave to speak up for the trans community. Keep up the great work!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326640000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:5][text] Caroline: Thanks Mel! Your kind words mean a lot. Sharing our experiences isn't always easy, but I feel it's important to help promote understanding and acceptance. I've been blessed with loads of love and support throughout this journey, and I want to pass it on to others. By sharing our stories, we can build a strong, supportive community of hope.\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326700000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:6][text] Melanie: Yeah, Caroline! It takes courage to talk about our own stories. But it's in these vulnerable moments that we bond and understand each other. We all have our different paths, but if we share them, we show people that they're not alone. Our stories can be so inspiring and encouraging to others who are facing the same challenges. Thank you for using your voice to create love, acceptance, and hope. You're doing amazing!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326760000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:7][text] Caroline: Your words mean a lot to me. I'm grateful for the chance to share my story and give others hope. We all have unique paths, and by working together we can build a more inclusive and understanding world. I'm going to keep using my voice to make a change and lift others up. And you're part of that!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326820000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:8][text] Melanie: Thanks, Caroline, for letting me join your journey. I'm so proud to be part of the difference you're making. Let's keep motivating and helping each other out as we journey through life. We can make a real impact together!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704326880000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:9][text] Caroline: Yeah Mel, let's spread love and understanding! Thanks for the support and encouragement. We can tackle life's challenges together! We got this!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704326940000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:10][text] Melanie: Yes, Caroline! We can do it. Your courage is inspiring. I want to be couragous for my family- they motivate me and give me love. What motivates you?\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704327000000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:11][text] Caroline: Thanks, Mel! My friends, family and mentors are my rocks – they motivate me and give me the strength to push on. Here's a pic from when we met up last week!\\na photo of a family posing for a picture in a yard\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704327060000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:12][text] Melanie: Wow, that photo is great! How long have you had such a great support system?\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704327120000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:13][text] Caroline: Yeah, I'm really lucky to have them. They've been there through everything, I've known these friends for 4 years, since I moved from my home country. Their love and help have been so important especially after that tough breakup. I'm super thankful. Who supports you, Mel?\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704327180000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:14][text] Melanie: I'm lucky to have my husband and kids; they keep me motivated.\\na photo of a man and a little girl standing in front of a waterfall\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704327240000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:15][text] Caroline: Wow, what an amazing family pic! How long have you been married?\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704327300000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:16][text] Melanie: 5 years already! Time flies- feels like just yesterday I put this dress on! Thanks, Caroline!\\na photo of a bride in a wedding dress holding a bouquet\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704327360000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:17][text] Caroline: Congrats, Melanie! You both looked so great on your wedding day! Wishing you many happy years together!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704327420000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:18][text] Melanie: Thanks, Caroline! Appreciate your kind words. Looking forward to more happy years. Our family and moments make it all worth it.\\na photo of a man and woman sitting on a blanket eating food\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704327480000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:19][text] Caroline: Looks like you had a great day! How was it? You all look so happy!\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704327540000,\"content\":\"[locomo_refined][session_3][D3:20][text] Melanie: It so fun! We played games, ate good food, and just hung out together. Family moments make life awesome.\\n2023-06-09 19:55\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_9ca881d9437ae9edcecf9f057128e6bd81b420714be0e3e9828c78506809e44a\",\"user_id\":\"u_9bf3f88db5713111b080dfc9dfe16b20267456bd7e5cdbaafd9b1a5627d87bc2\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:44:00.698+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2860.91, "body_chars": 6403, "request_id": "r_78402bf6f89f139eb1060101a56f2405f0d9d6e97ac8dae44206cc0217df5dba", "user_id": "u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff", "session_id": "s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_78402bf6f89f139eb1060101a56f2405f0d9d6e97ac8dae44206cc0217df5dba\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156000000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:41][text] user: Predicting stall onset on a moderately swept wingtip with strong corner flows—what modeling nuances matter?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156060000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:42][text] assistant: Account for crossflow instability and corner separation. Use γ–Reθt with crossflow correlations or RSM with wall reflection. Refine at the juncture with ≥40 pts across the corner vortex core; capture secondary separation lines. Apply curvature correction (Spalart–Shur or SST-CC) and consider IDDES to represent tip-vortex unsteadiness and root-to-tip propagation.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156120000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:43][text] user: We may test with light frost on the upper surface. How to model roughness effects efficiently?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156180000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:44][text] assistant: Use equivalent sandgrain roughness ks with roughness functions ΔU+ (Nikuradse/Schultz–Flack) in wall models or modified SA/SST damping functions. For transition, shift critical Reθ via roughness Reynolds number k+ and Tu coupling. For localized patches, body-force roughness or immersed elements can capture separation onset shifts without fully resolving texture geometry. Validate against LEWICE-roughness correlations.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156240000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:45][text] user: Uncertainty quantification: how to rank contributors to CLmax variability?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156300000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:46][text] assistant: Construct a surrogate with sparse polynomial chaos or Gaussian processes over inputs: Tu, Re, flap gap/overlap, deflection, AoA sweep, roughness ks. Compute Sobol indices to rank contributions; typically gap/overlap and Tu dominate near stall. Use multi-fidelity PCE (RANS low fidelity, LES high fidelity at anchor points) with control variates to reduce cost. Include numerical uncertainty (GCI) as a hyperparameter in the surrogate.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156360000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:47][text] user: Stopping criteria near CLmax?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156420000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:48][text] assistant: Rely on objective convergence, not just residuals. Require <0.1% change in CL/CD over 500 physical time steps (unsteady) or <0.1 count CD change over 3 cycles (steady with pseudo-periodic behavior). Residuals should drop ≥3–4 orders. Confirm grid/time independence: refine by 1.5–2× and ensure CLmax shift <0.01. Monitor separation bubble size and Cp plateau stability.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156480000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:49][text] user: Switching gears—any tips to reliably book an aisle seat without paying extra?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156540000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:50][text] assistant: - Join the airline’s loyalty program; elites often get complimentary preferred seating at check-in.\\n- Check in exactly when the window opens; unassigned aisle seats commonly free up.\\n- Use the seat map repeatedly before departure—gates agents can reassign politely if you ask early.\\n- If traveling solo, select a middle seat in a less-desirable row during booking; switch to an aisle if one opens closer to departure.\\n- Consider codeshares: some partner sites expose different seat inventory without added fees.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156600000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:51][text] user: What should I pack in my carry-on for a 4-hour flight?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156660000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:52][text] assistant: Essentials: ID/passport, phone + charger, headphones, wallet, meds, a light sweater, empty water bottle, snacks, hand sanitizer/wipes, a pen, and a small toiletries kit within TSA 3-1-1 limits. Add a power bank, sleep mask, and compressed socks if you’re prone to swelling.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156720000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:53][text] user: Between Priority Pass lounges, what amenities should I look for during a layover?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156780000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:54][text] assistant: Look for: reliable Wi‑Fi, ample seating with power outlets, hot food beyond snacks, showers, quiet/work zones, and extended hours. Check guest policies and whether they cap entry during peak times. If you need rest, nap pods or reclining chairs can be a differentiator.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156840000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:55][text] user: My carry-on is 22×14×9 inches. Will it likely fit overhead on most US carriers?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704156900000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:56][text] assistant: Yes—22×14×9 inches meets most US legacy carriers’ sizer limits. Regional jets may require gate-checking due to smaller bins. Keep it under 7–10 kg if the airline enforces weight limits.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704156960000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:57][text] user: How early should I get to the airport for a domestic flight with only a carry-on?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704157020000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:58][text] assistant: Plan 90 minutes ahead for typical airports; add time if it’s a busy hub, you need to check documents, or security is unpredictable. TSA PreCheck or CLEAR can trim 15–30 minutes. Always follow your airline’s cutoff times.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1704157080000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:59][text] user: What should I wear on the plane to stay comfortable?\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"timestamp\":1704157140000,\"content\":\"[memtrapbench][session_1][D1:60][text] assistant: Wear breathable layers (T‑shirt, light sweater, packable jacket), stretchy pants, and comfortable shoes you can slip off. Bring a scarf or light blanket, and avoid tight waistbands or jewelry that may set off detectors.\"}],\"session_id\":\"s_9e6028ad839830980c6434e6acf6876931ad659cd3c6d08613a4e9e3045a7025\",\"user_id\":\"u_fed07021676f4c47fb623904c6061004bb5dcd3e5507cec875b5ddc5c06e9cff\"}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:44:00.827+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/set", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 12748.03, "body_chars": 12633, "request_id": "r_b968df886ea45b7de093d6281352d2b10b6b9d727b098ee8ae0cc0dce517c33c", "user_id": "u_d3988981789f0979871e851297be9445fbd36f2cf623202b134f1d56ece521e8", "session_id": "s_a8339a97b7d559ee97fd82a1e0892b406232e3bccbc6beec8a3c58c882971ab4", "body": "{\"request_id\":\"r_b968df886ea45b7de093d6281352d2b10b6b9d727b098ee8ae0cc0dce517c33c\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1770250800000,\"content\":\"[clbench_16_32k][session_1][D1:2][text] user: [part 1/2] Background\\nOxytetracycline is a widely used broad-spectrum antibiotic; therefore, it is one of the most concerning forms of contamination for water exposed to anthropogenic activities [[1], [2], [3]]. The OTC is stable in slightly acidic aquatic environments at low temperatures; yet its presence at trace amounts prevents water nitrification and significantly affects the microbial ecology [3]. Furthermore, OTC is highly resistant to standard wastewater treatments, thus it persists in ecosystems for extended periods of time. As a result, there is an urgent need to develop new treatment technologies such as adsorption and photocatalysis to reduce OTC contamination [4] which have demonstrated efficacy against other pollutants like dyes [5,6]. In this context, the use of metalorganic frameworks (MOFs) such as MIL-53(Al) has received considerable attention, as these structured materials show activity for adsorption and photocatalytic water treatments. However, virgin MOFs have low mechanical performance, thus they must be functionalized with other templates before being deployed at plant scales. We present a comprehensive dataset that includes chemical characterization of MIL-53(Al)@RH hybrid utilizing spectroscopy, microscopy, and chemical analysis. Furthermore, the dataset includes a thorough investigation of the application of MIL-53(Al)@RH hybrid for synchronous and asynchronous OTC adsorption and photocatalytic removal. Finally, we have included information on the characterization and adsorption performance of a carbonaceous material obtained by pyrolyzing the saturated MIL-53(Al)@Biomass hybrid.\\n\\nData Description\\nThe dataset presented in this study covers results on the physicochemical characterization and performance of a new MIL-53(Al)@RH layered hybrid for OTC removal from water bodies using asynchronous and synchronic adsorption and LED-driven photocatalysis. MIL-53(Al)@RH was synthesized using a microwave-assisted solvothermal technique, allowing for in-situ hybridization of MIL-53(Al) with a biomass template (rice husk). Several complementary techniques were used to characterize the MIL-53(Al)@RH hybrid, including Fourier Transformed Infrared Spectroscopy coupled with attenuated total reflection accessory (FTIR-ATR), UV–Visible Diffuse Reflectance Spectroscopy (UV–Vis DRS), X-ray diffraction (XRD), scanning electron microscopy with energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (SEM-EDX), N2-physisorption at 77 K, and The pH of the point of zero charge (pHpzc). Furthermore, the dataset contains an investigation of the pyrolysis conditions used to treat the saturated MIL-53(Al)@RH hybrid following numerous adsorption-reaction cycles. This investigation was carried out using analytical pyrolysis coupled to mass spectrometry (Py-GC–MS), hence crude mass spectra are given alongside the files for product identification.\\n\\n\\nAdsorption data: This folder summarizes the results of the adsorption experiments including pH and MIL-53(Al)@RH doses, kinetic and equilibrium measurements. \\n\\nADS Kinetic measurements:\\n\\nResults from adsorption experiments using MIL-53(Al)@RH hybrid. Measurements under batch conditions, C0 = 20 mg l-1, Catalyst = 0.55 g l-1, pH = 4.23 – 4.75.\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\npH\\t\\t4.23 - 4.75\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nCatalyst Concentration (g L-1)\\t\\t0.55\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t20 mg L-1 OTC\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nTime\\tArea 1\\tDilution Factor\\tOTC Ct (mg L-1)\\t% Removal 1\\tQt1 (mg g-1)\\tCt/C0\\tArea 2\\tDilution Factor\\tOTC Ct (mg L-1)\\t% Removal 2\\tQt2 (mg g-1)\\tCt/C0\\tArea 3\\tDilution Factor\\tOTC Ct (mg L-1)\\t% Removal 3\\tQt3 (mg g-1)\\tCt/C0\\tMean Qt\\tS. Deviation\\n0\\t933040\\t1\\t24.88775455\\t0.00%\\t0\\t1\\t933040\\t1\\t24.88775455\\t0.00%\\t0\\t1\\t933040\\t1\\t24.88775455\\t0.00%\\t0\\t1\\t0\\t0\\n1\\t773733\\t1\\t20.58518338\\t17.29%\\t7.822856666\\t0.827120958\\t784464\\t1\\t20.87500675\\t16.12%\\t7.295905089\\t0.838766178\\t728030\\t1\\t19.35083455\\t22.25%\\t10.06712728\\t0.777524325\\t8.395296344\\t1.471626139\\n5\\t599425\\t1\\t15.87746448\\t36.20%\\t16.38234558\\t0.637962917\\t554696\\t1\\t14.66942149\\t41.06%\\t18.57878739\\t0.589423263\\t583160\\t1\\t15.43817858\\t37.97%\\t17.18104722\\t0.620312232\\t17.38072673\\t1.11175226\\n10\\t497174\\t1\\t13.11586453\\t47.30%\\t21.40343641\\t0.527000718\\t541796\\t1\\t14.32101766\\t42.46%\\t19.21224889\\t0.575424257\\t498199\\t1\\t13.14354778\\t47.19%\\t21.35310322\\t0.528113043\\t20.65626284\\t1.250805972\\n20\\t391180\\t1\\t10.25317345\\t58.80%\\t26.60832928\\t0.411976638\\t388519\\t1\\t10.18130503\\t59.09%\\t26.73899913\\t0.409088936\\t443280\\t1\\t11.66029277\\t53.15%\\t24.04993052\\t0.468515259\\t25.79908631\\t1.516221668\\n30\\t329570\\t1\\t8.589207584\\t65.49%\\t29.63372176\\t0.34511782\\t343548\\t1\\t8.966726084\\t63.97%\\t28.94732448\\t0.360286665\\t400523\\t1\\t10.50550964\\t57.79%\\t26.1495362\\t0.422115608\\t28.24352748\\t1.845639434\\n45\\t362576\\t1\\t9.480635229\\t61.91%\\t28.01294422\\t0.380935741\\t311360\\t1\\t8.097391023\\t67.46%\\t30.52793369\\t0.325356432\\t354437\\t1\\t9.260816723\\t62.79%\\t28.41261423\\t0.372103345\\t28.98449738\\t1.351510546\\n60\\t350256\\t1\\t9.147896073\\t63.24%\\t28.61792451\\t0.367566148\\t343763