{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:45:11.088+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/get", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 628.91, "body_chars": 2386, "user_id": "u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1", "query": "What does the camera’s movement and the crowding into the elevator most strongly imply about how the scene is framing the setting?\n\nA. It is signaling that the scene is shifting away from court activity toward administrative offices, with the elevator serving as a staff-only passage.\nB. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub, but with the elevator functioning mainly as the primary passage to administrative floors rather than to courtrooms.\nC. It is emphasizing a confined, private confrontation about to happen inside a single elevator, rather than the building’s broader function.\nD. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub where people are being funneled from a public lobby into more specialized spaces.\nE. It is indicating that the main action will occur outside the courthouse, using the interior only as a brief transition.\nF. It is establishing the courthouse as a hectic, multi-courtroom hub where the camera lingers on one elevator because it’s repeatedly delayed by people squeezing in, implying a bottlenecked access point that’s central to navigating the building.\n\nPlease provide the option corresponding to the only correct answer, enclosed in parentheses, e.g., (X).", "top_k": 100, "body": "{\"query\":\"What does the camera’s movement and the crowding into the elevator most strongly imply about how the scene is framing the setting?\\n\\nA. It is signaling that the scene is shifting away from court activity toward administrative offices, with the elevator serving as a staff-only passage.\\nB. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub, but with the elevator functioning mainly as the primary passage to administrative floors rather than to courtrooms.\\nC. It is emphasizing a confined, private confrontation about to happen inside a single elevator, rather than the building’s broader function.\\nD. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub where people are being funneled from a public lobby into more specialized spaces.\\nE. It is indicating that the main action will occur outside the courthouse, using the interior only as a brief transition.\\nF. It is establishing the courthouse as a hectic, multi-courtroom hub where the camera lingers on one elevator because it’s repeatedly delayed by people squeezing in, implying a bottlenecked access point that’s central to navigating the building.\\n\\nPlease provide the option corresponding to the only correct answer, enclosed in parentheses, e.g., (X).\",\"user_id\":\"u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1\",\"top_k\":100,\"options\":[\"A. It is signaling that the scene is shifting away from court activity toward administrative offices, with the elevator serving as a staff-only passage.\",\"B. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub, but with the elevator functioning mainly as the primary passage to administrative floors rather than to courtrooms.\",\"C. It is emphasizing a confined, private confrontation about to happen inside a single elevator, rather than the building’s broader function.\",\"D. It is establishing the courthouse as a busy, multi-courtroom hub where people are being funneled from a public lobby into more specialized spaces.\",\"E. It is indicating that the main action will occur outside the courthouse, using the interior only as a brief transition.\",\"F. It is establishing the courthouse as a hectic, multi-courtroom hub where the camera lingers on one elevator because it’s repeatedly delayed by people squeezing in, implying a bottlenecked access point that’s central to navigating the building.\"]}"}
