{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:45:11.437+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/get", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 980.5, "body_chars": 2141, "user_id": "u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1", "query": "What does the Foreman’s behavior most strongly indicate about his role in the group’s decision-making at that moment?\n\nA. He is rejecting #8’s proposal as unfair and reasserting open voting to preserve transparency and accountability.\nB. He is disengaged from the process, leaving the decision entirely to #8 by refusing to participate in any vote.\nC. He is covertly siding with #8 and using his position to steer the group toward a predetermined reversal of the verdict.\nD. He is supporting #8’s proposal because he personally doubts the guilty verdict, and he uses the secret ballot mainly as a way to test whether any juror shares that doubt without risking social pressure.\nE. He is acting primarily as a procedural facilitator, enforcing a voting method that protects anonymity and legitimizes the outcome.\nF. He is actively aligning with #8 and subtly steering the group toward acquittal by participating in the secret ballot himself and managing the first slip to shape how the vote is perceived.\n\nPlease provide the option corresponding to the only correct answer, enclosed in parentheses, e.g., (X).", "top_k": 100, "body": "{\"query\":\"What does the Foreman’s behavior most strongly indicate about his role in the group’s decision-making at that moment?\\n\\nA. He is rejecting #8’s proposal as unfair and reasserting open voting to preserve transparency and accountability.\\nB. He is disengaged from the process, leaving the decision entirely to #8 by refusing to participate in any vote.\\nC. He is covertly siding with #8 and using his position to steer the group toward a predetermined reversal of the verdict.\\nD. He is supporting #8’s proposal because he personally doubts the guilty verdict, and he uses the secret ballot mainly as a way to test whether any juror shares that doubt without risking social pressure.\\nE. He is acting primarily as a procedural facilitator, enforcing a voting method that protects anonymity and legitimizes the outcome.\\nF. He is actively aligning with #8 and subtly steering the group toward acquittal by participating in the secret ballot himself and managing the first slip to shape how the vote is perceived.\\n\\nPlease provide the option corresponding to the only correct answer, enclosed in parentheses, e.g., (X).\",\"user_id\":\"u_40683a81aadb2e617cbde99e9ad516d4732d1f83d34372efaae3037f692bf2f1\",\"top_k\":100,\"options\":[\"A. He is rejecting #8’s proposal as unfair and reasserting open voting to preserve transparency and accountability.\",\"B. He is disengaged from the process, leaving the decision entirely to #8 by refusing to participate in any vote.\",\"C. He is covertly siding with #8 and using his position to steer the group toward a predetermined reversal of the verdict.\",\"D. He is supporting #8’s proposal because he personally doubts the guilty verdict, and he uses the secret ballot mainly as a way to test whether any juror shares that doubt without risking social pressure.\",\"E. He is acting primarily as a procedural facilitator, enforcing a voting method that protects anonymity and legitimizes the outcome.\",\"F. He is actively aligning with #8 and subtly steering the group toward acquittal by participating in the secret ballot himself and managing the first slip to shape how the vote is perceived.\"]}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:45:11.866+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/get", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 1386.12, "body_chars": 1328, "user_id": "u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c", "query": "What are some ways to make my weekend reading time feel more relaxing and immersive?", "top_k": 100, "body": "{\"query\":\"What are some ways to make my weekend reading time feel more relaxing and immersive?\",\"user_id\":\"u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c\",\"top_k\":100,\"options\":[\"Settle in with your favorite printed book in a cozy nook, maybe near a sunny window or with a soft lamp, and add a warm drink to sip on. Consider creating a small ritual, like lighting a candle before you open the pages, to make the time feel more special and immersive.\",\"Settle in with your favorite e-book on a tablet in a cozy nook, maybe near a sunny window or with a soft lamp, and add a warm drink to sip on. Consider creating a small ritual, like lighting a candle before you start swiping through the pages, to make the time feel more special and immersive.\",\"Settle in with something you enjoy reading in a comfortable spot, maybe near a sunny window or with a soft lamp, and add a warm drink to sip on. Consider creating a small ritual, like lighting a candle before you begin, to make the time feel more special and immersive.\",\"Settle in with your favorite audiobook playing in the background, perhaps while sitting in your favorite chair, and add a warm drink to sip on. Consider creating a small ritual, like lighting a candle before you put on your headphones, to make the time feel more special and immersive.\"]}"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T09:45:12.066+00:00", "method": "POST", "path": "/get", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 1607.26, "body_chars": 1633, "user_id": "u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c", "query": "What kind of warm-up should I do before a casual game of pickup basketball?", "top_k": 100, "body": "{\"query\":\"What kind of warm-up should I do before a casual game of pickup basketball?\",\"user_id\":\"u_ec3274fa810aa5d684e571c0cb5c7b8fb5a3c6b8058cec6e79280303e1a4847c\",\"top_k\":100,\"options\":[\"Given your preference for early morning workouts, start with 5–10 minutes of brisk walking or light jogging to wake your body up, then move into dynamic stretches like arm circles and walking lunges. Add a few short sprints to sharpen your reaction time. Finish with some game-related movements like layup drills to get into a basketball mindset.\",\"Before a casual pickup game, start with 5–10 minutes of light jogging or cycling to increase your heart rate. Follow with dynamic stretches like lunges, high knees, and butt kicks to loosen your muscles. End with a few basketball movements—like dribbling drills or short layups—so you’re ready for the pace of the game.\",\"Since you likely have a competitive streak from your high school sports background, start with 5–10 minutes of jogging to loosen up, then add dynamic stretches like lunges and high knees. Work in some quick footwork drills to prime agility. Wrap up with basketball-specific warm-up shots to tap into that old athlete rhythm.\",\"Given your history of an old left knee ligament tear, start with 5–10 minutes of light jogging or cycling to get blood flowing, then focus on dynamic leg stretches like high knees and butt kicks. Incorporate gentle lateral shuffles and a few bodyweight squats to activate your quads and hamstrings. Finish with some light basketball-specific movements, like dribbling while side-stepping, to prep the knee for game-like motions.\"]}"}
